@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# V170 Manual Bank Payout Atomicity
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.170-manual-bank-payout-atomicity`
+
+## Change
+
+Manual Company Bank payouts now require the complete bank transaction and audit
+evidence chain before a provider payout can become `succeeded`, a withdrawal can
+become `paid`, or its wallet reservation can be released.
+
+The payout-start audit is created before the provider and withdrawal move to
+`processing`. Its identifier is bound to a fresh authorization value. A primary
+key collision therefore leaves the provider `prepared`, the withdrawal
+`approved`, and the full wallet hold intact so the operation can be retried.
+
+The paid audit also uses a fresh identifier. Evidence is accepted only when
+exactly one audit row matches the bank transaction's event, target and recording
+user, and that audit timestamp equals the bank transaction timestamp. A missing,
+duplicated or conflicting receipt fails closed and never releases the hold.
+
+## Retry and recovery behavior
+
+An identical confirmation reuses the existing bank transaction. If a paid-audit
+identifier collides with an unrelated row, the first request moves the payout to
+review and keeps the withdrawal and hold unchanged. A later request with the
+same evidence can create a new audit identifier and finish exactly once.
+Different bank evidence remains a conflict and cannot debit or release funds.
+
+The confirmation route can also repair the legacy partial state where the
+provider payout is already `succeeded/accepted` but the withdrawal remains
+`processing` and its wallet reservation remains held. Repair is allowed only
+when the existing bank transaction, provider reference, amount, currency,
+account, reference, proof hash and occurrence time all match. It attaches the
+missing unique audit evidence, completes the withdrawal, and releases the hold
+once. Any mismatch remains blocked for reconciliation.
+
+## Verification
+
+- targeted SQLite manual-bank suite: 19/19 passed;
+- related regression checks: 74/74 passed;
+- full regression: 1,412/1,412 passed;
+- isolated PostgreSQL 18 manual-bank suite: 6/6 passed, including concurrent
+  confirmation, legacy deterministic audit-ID collisions, and rollback-only
+  backup/restore verification;
+- TypeScript, lint and diff checks passed;
+- independent review found no blocker.
+
+## Scope
+
+- no schema migration, table, column or backup-contract change;
+- latest migration remains `0123-guard-function-schema-binding`;
+- backup schema remains `0122-acceptance-ledger-integrity` with 76 tables;
+- no live payment-provider, game-provider, customer-money or wallet call was
+  made during validation;
+- new deposits, new payouts, new game launches, real payments, live games and
+  production readiness remain disabled pending external acceptance.
